course: dictionary
lesson: 6604
title: The prefix non-
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A prefix is a few letters added to the start of a word to change its meaning. Non- means not or without. Add it to a word and you get the opposite, or something that lacks that thing: fiction is made-up stories, so non-fiction is true facts.
explain: Look at «Non merci is a polite way to say no.» Here non is a French word that means no. It is not the English prefix. The words around it give the clue: merci means thank you, so the sentence is French. Always check which meaning fits the context.
explain: When you meet non- in English, split the word into two parts: non + stop gives non-stop, which means without stopping. Check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence. A non-stop flight is a flight with no stops on the way.
fact: Non- is a prefix: it is put at the start of a word and cannot stand alone.
fact: Non- means not or without.
fact: Most words with non- are written with a hyphen, such as non-fiction, non-stop and non-living.
fact: Non-fiction books tell true facts, unlike fiction, which is made up.
fact: Non-living things are not alive. «Non merci» is French and means no thanks, so it is a different word that only looks the same.
exercise: What does non- mean at the start of a word? | Very big | *Not or without | Under | Again
exercise: A non-fiction book tells you what? | Jokes only | Songs | *True facts | Made-up stories
exercise: «Non merci is a polite way to say no.» What does non mean in this sentence? | Nothing at all | Yes | Thank you | *No
test: Which word means without stopping? | *non-stop | non-fiction | non-living | non-toxic
test: What does non-living mean? | Living for ever | *Not alive | Lost in the woods | Very alive
exam: Pupil asks: Can non- stand alone as a word in English? | No, it means very | Yes, it is always French | Yes, it means not | *No, it is a prefix and goes at the start of another word
